[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked **known**: one bug, one fix queued — the parser reads
dates month first. The 412 reports reached it by [subject match alone](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject),
so nobody read the bodies after the merge. Read them and the ticket is not one problem. It is three,
and the queued fix only touches the first.

## What the merge actually holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table groups by cause from the code, not by subject. Two causes fall out — `parser` and `hint` —
and a footnote marks reports that are not a swap at all. Those three groups are three separate
problems, with three separate fixes.

## Problem 1 — the shared parser reads dates month first

The `sched-prod` parser reads every stored date as `MM/DD`. A day-first tenant's `07/04` (7 April)
comes back as 4 July: day and month trade places. This is the known bug, and it is the bulk of the
ticket. It reaches the desk through every channel and every tenant, because every tenant on file
writes the day first. Fix the parser and these stop.

<Callout kind="warn">
This is the only problem the queued fix addresses. Problems 2 and 3 survive it.
</Callout>

## Problem 2 — booking-v3 prints the wrong date hint

Under its date field, the **booking-v3** form prints `MM/DD/YYYY`. A day-first tenant's staff follow
the hint and type the month first; the form then stores the date read their way, day first — so it
is swapped before it ever reaches the parser. Same wrong day on the invite, different root cause.
These come only through the **form**, and only from the three tenants on booking-v3
(alder.physio, copper.studio, pale.harbour). The parser fix does nothing here: the fix is the form's
hint. `causeOf` already separates them — `channel === 'form'` on a `MM`-hint form is tagged `hint`,
not `parser`.

## Problem 3 — a one-day shift, not a swap

A handful of reports describe a date that is **one day off**, not month-and-day swapped
(`desk-notes.json` → `oneDayMove`, shown in the footnote above). A swap cannot produce them:

- *"Every booking in June is one day off. Only June."* — one month, one day: a DST boundary.
- *"Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday. Same meeting."* — a time zone, not a locale.
- *"The invite arrived before I made the booking."* — a UTC offset on the send.

The desk filed these under `parser` by tenant and footnoted them. They are a day-boundary / time-zone
bug. Fixing the parser and the form hint leaves every one of them live.

## Since April

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

Reports have arrived steadily since April and are still arriving. The ticket being "known" did not
stop the queue, because two of its three problems were never worked.

## The split

One ticket per problem, each counting the reports it covers — the `parser` group (379) minus the
five one-day reports footnoted above, plus the `hint` group (33) and the five:

| ticket | problem | reports |
|--------|---------|--------:|
| 1 | parser reads dates month first | 374 |
| 2 | booking-v3 prints the wrong date hint | 33 |
| 3 | one-day / time-zone shift | 5 |

374 + 33 + 5 = 412. The tickets are filed as issues in this repo.

